# livepeer is liveprobe's second half -- the other party, in its own process -- and its build output
# has the same shape and the same 36 MB: README.md tells an operator to `go build -o livepeer.exe .`
# in this tracked directory, and the two unix names are the ones liveprobe's own build recipe would
# give it. Ignored before the first `git add .` here rather than after it. Carried from the core
# SDK's .gitignore (urnetwork/sdk b8e0da26, lines 10-15), whose rules the sdk removal drops with the
# directory.
/livepeer
/livepeer-arm64
*.exe
